From: AX50 port
Subject: [PATCH] wave: define the HT TX MCS set for mac80211 station interfaces

The shared cfg80211 templates leave tx_params zero. mac80211 then skips
intersecting the HT RX MCS masks, and the WAVE station connection code
omits STA_FLAGS_11n because that negotiated mask is empty. A 2.4 GHz
uplink is consequently restricted to legacy rates.

Define the TX set on the station wiphy after its per-radio RX masks have
been populated. TX and RX use the same supported stream count. Leave
the separately registered AP wiphy and its hostapd capabilities unchanged.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/mac80211.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/mac80211.c
@@ -2178,7 +2178,7 @@
 int __MTLK_IFUNC
 wv_ieee80211_setup_register (struct device *dev, wv_mac80211_t *mac80211, mtlk_handle_t hw_handle)
 {
-  int ret;
+  int ret, band;
   struct ieee80211_hw *hw = mac80211->mac80211_hw;
   u32 num_sts = WV_SUPP_NUM_STS; /* should get overwritten */
 
@@ -2260,6 +2260,17 @@
   if (ret != MTLK_ERR_OK)
     return ret;
 
+  /* mac80211 needs TX_DEFINED to negotiate the peer's HT MCS mask.
+   * These station-only band copies already contain the radio's RX MCS
+   * masks; TX supports the same streams. Do not alter the AP templates.
+   */
+  for (band = 0; band < NUM_SUPPORTED_BANDS; band++) {
+    struct ieee80211_supported_band *sband = hw->wiphy->bands[band];
+
+    if (sband && sband->ht_cap.ht_supported)
+      sband->ht_cap.mcs.tx_params |= IEEE80211_HT_MCS_TX_DEFINED;
+  }
+
   /* Setting up passive scan on radar channels */
   wv_ieee80211_mark_ch_for_passive_scan(hw->wiphy);
 
